  {
    "id": "ex-epewg22d",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "companion",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "What does `private constructor` plus a companion `of` guarantee?",
    "hint": "Every way in.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "That sessions are created faster",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Not the point."
      },
      {
        "text": "That only one session ever exists",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Two were created."
      },
      {
        "text": "Every session passes `of`'s checks",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: there is no other door."
      },
      {
        "text": "That Java code cannot use the class",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Java can call the companion's functions."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-825hp2hc",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "const-and-jvm",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "What did `javap` show about where `of` is compiled?",
    "hint": "Two classes were listed.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "As a static method on `Session`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Only with `@JvmStatic`."
      },
      {
        "text": "On the inner class `Session$Companion`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "In `CompanionKt`, with `main`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That holds top-level functions."
      },
      {
        "text": "Nowhere: companion functions are inlined",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "They are ordinary methods."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-zegp9ytd",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "const-and-jvm",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Which of these is refused as a `const val`?",
    "hint": "Known when the program is compiled.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`const val MAX_MINUTES = 600`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A literal `Int`: allowed."
      },
      {
        "text": "`const val APP = \"planner\"`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A literal `String`: allowed."
      },
      {
        "text": "`const val TODAY = LocalDate.now()`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: its value is only known at run time."
      },
      {
        "text": "`const val STRICT = true`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A literal `Boolean`: allowed."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-d59f8xwv",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "const-and-jvm",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "After adding `@JvmStatic` to `of`, what changes for Kotlin code that calls `Session.of(…)`?",
    "hint": "What do the `@Jvm…` annotations change?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "It must now write `Session.Companion.of(…)`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That was Java's form before."
      },
      {
        "text": "The call becomes faster, as it skips the companion",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "The static method forwards to the companion."
      },
      {
        "text": "Nothing",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: only what Java sees changes."
      },
      {
        "text": "It no longer compiles until imports are added",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Nothing breaks."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-rmmdk4zd",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "object-expressions",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "What is `object : Comparator<String> { … }`?",
    "hint": "Java's anonymous class.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "A singleton named `Comparator`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It has no name and is not shared."
      },
      {
        "text": "A new unnamed object implementing `Comparator`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "A companion object of `String`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It belongs to no class."
      },
      {
        "text": "A data object comparing strings",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "No `data` and no single instance."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-hghestt6",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "object-expressions",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "When does an object expression earn its place over a lambda?",
    "hint": "One method fits in a lambda.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "Whenever a Java interface is involved",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "`Comparator` is Java, and a lambda worked."
      },
      {
        "text": "With several methods to implement, or state of its own",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "When the code must run faster",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Not the criterion."
      },
      {
        "text": "When the object will be compared with `===`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Unrelated."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-1rp01kdy",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "data-object",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "`println(WeekState.Empty)`, where `Empty` is a `data object`. What prints?",
    "hint": "The visible difference.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`Empty`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: its name."
      },
      {
        "text": "`WeekState$Empty@` and a hash code",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That is a plain `object`."
      },
      {
        "text": "`Empty()`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "There are no parentheses: it has no properties."
      },
      {
        "text": "Nothing, since it has no data",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It prints its name."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-s1ss55h7",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "data-object",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "In a sealed hierarchy, which declaration does the section recommend for a case with no data?",
    "hint": "One word more than `object`.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`class Empty : WeekState`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A class makes a new instance each time."
      },
      {
        "text": "`object Empty : WeekState`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It works, and prints a hash code."
      },
      {
        "text": "`data class Empty() : WeekState`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A data class needs a property."
      },
      {
        "text": "`data object Empty : WeekState`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-kzxwccwg",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "singletons-cost",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "`checkOneSession()` then `checkEmptyWeek()` failed; in the other order both passed. Why?",
    "hint": "What do the two checks share?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`check` caches its results",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It has no cache."
      },
      {
        "text": "Both used the one global `Planner`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: the first left 45 minutes behind."
      },
      {
        "text": "The JVM runs functions in random order",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "`main` ran them in the written order."
      },
      {
        "text": "`checkEmptyWeek` has a bug",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It is correct on its own."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-78xjggkp",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "singletons-cost",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "What fixed the order dependence?",
    "hint": "Dependency injection in its simplest form.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "Clearing the list at the end of each check",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That helps until one check forgets, or fails before clearing."
      },
      {
        "text": "Making `sessions` a `val`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It was a `val`; the list itself changed."
      },
      {
        "text": "A `Planner` class, a new one per check",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "Calling the checks in alphabetical order",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That hides the problem."
      }
    ]
  },
